#+TITLE: type-of-defun-subr-or-usubr -- (type f) of a DEFUN'd function was SUBR on AutoCAD and BricsCAD in the type-symbols probe, USUBR in clautolisp
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-23

* Symptom

Found reconciling type-symbols-print-lowercase-on-autocad (probe suite
type-symbols, probes/sources/probe-type-symbols.lsp; AutoCAD 2022 run
20261023T074943Z, BricsCAD V25 20261023T075150Z, V26 20261023T031215Z):
the TYPE of a function defined with DEFUN in the probe file was SUBR on
every vendor, where clautolisp answers USUBR.

USUBR is documented for a user-defined function loaded from source;
SUBR for a built-in or a COMPILED (.fas / .vlx, or vlisp-compiled)
function. The probe runner may load the probe sources compiled, or the
vendor may compile DEFUNs on LOAD -- not known.

* To do

Probe: (defun f () 1) typed at the command line, in a plain .lsp loaded
with LOAD, and via alfe -l / -x; record (type f) and (type (function
f)), plus (type car). Then decide whether clautolisp's USUBR needs a
per-situation answer (compiled-function / load path) -- see
clautolisp's own compiled bodies, which are not SUBRs today.

* Batched probe prepared 2026-10-29 (branch prep-pending-probes)

probes/sources/probe-pending-divergences.lsp (suite "pending-divergences",
group type-of-fn) captures this on real hardware. Run it via
probe:suite:{autocad,bricscad}:windows / :macos when the Windows runner is next
online (one session covers all three data-blocked issues). clautolisp baseline
validated 2026-10-29.
